From bfea5adbee8db99195698f30e46fb9d132fd770f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:00:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui,app): setup alignment composes on the current pose,
 one flow, readable picks (#738)

- Laying the part on a face or on three points reads the pick through the
  setup's held alignment and composes the lay onto it
  (pick::lay_on_plane_in / lay_on_points_in); a re-applied pick is a zero
  step. Each move stays one AlignPartToSetup undo step.
- The Part alignment row is one step of the flow: presets and "Turn by"
  turn the part from where it sits now (CommandKind::TurnPart ->
  AlignPartToSetup::turn_by -> setup_turn::turned_by); "As modelled" is
  the one reset. Tooltips describe the flow.
- Pick status reads "1 face selected", "2 points selected", "1 edge
  selected" (ui::pick_words); no internal feature ids on the rows or in
  pick refusals.
- The collecting draft's picks paint as filled semi-transparent faces,
  round filled point discs and bold 4 px edges (ui::align_pick_viz).
- Split: commands/setup_align.rs's following-stock half moves to
  commands/align_stock.rs; state.rs's alignment arms move to
  state_align.rs.

Fixes #738

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
